Nina (docs): Heads up, our error-ref page still trips up folks — proposal: add a small decision graphic + two tiny SDK snippets (JS/Python) for safe retry + Retry-After handling.
Omar (eng-runtime): Good call. Diagram needs to show order: client retry -> middleware trim/summarize -> model variant fallback -> region failover. Also mark streaming as a special case.
Liu (devex): I can drop a Mermaid block into the PR. Quick draft: ```mermaid
flowchart LR
  Req[Request] --> E{Error type}
  E -- 429 --> Retry[Client retry + backoff]
  E -- timeout --> Trim[Trim/summarize & retry]
  Retry --> Check{Still failing?}
  Check -- yes --> Model[Fallback: smaller/quantized model]
  Model --> Region[Regional failover]
  Check -- no --> OK[Success]
```
Hannah (eng-ml): Add a short note about KV cache compatibility when switching to quantized modelssome quantizations change key sizes; recommend try-reuse then cold-start fallback.
Nina (docs): I'll open the PR and include a short FAQ blurb: "When should I retry vs trim?" Answer: start with client retry+backoff; if persistent, enable trim or smaller model; contact support if wide-spread.
Liu (devex): Draft JS snippet (will refine in PR): ```js
async function fetchWithRetry(req, attempts=4){
  for(let i=0;i<attempts;i++){
    const r = await fetch(req);
    if(r.status===429){
      const ra = parseInt(r.headers.get('Retry-After')||'0',10);
      const wait = ra>0? ra*1000 : Math.min(60000, (2**i)*100 + Math.random()*200);
      await new Promise(s=>setTimeout(s, wait));
      continue;
    }
    return r;
  }
  throw new Error('max-retries');
}
```
Hannah (eng-ml): I'll add a tiny pseudo for trim middleware and a note about preserving instruction tokens.
Omar (eng-runtime): For streaming, call out resume tokens / X-Resume-Offset header; retries must preserve idempotency. I'll add a review note in the PR.
